(a) No license issued under this article shall be suspended, revoked or placed on probation with or without conditions, except for due cause as defined in subsection (b) hereof and only after a hearing before the board of commissioners upon a prior written notice to the licensee of the time, place and purpose of such hearing and a statement of the reason why the license may be suspended or revoked. Three (3) days' notice shall be deemed reasonable, but shorter or longer periods of notice shall be authorized as the board of commissioners may deem the circumstances justify.
(b) "Due cause" for the suspension or revocation of such license shall consist of any of the following:
(1) A licensee commits a deceptive business practice when he: (i) uses or possesses a false weight, measure or any other device for falsely determining or recording any quality or quantity in connection with any sale or service; (ii) sells, offers, exposes for sale or delivers less than the represented quality or quantity; (iii) takes or attempts to take more than the represented quality or quantity of any commodity when, as buyer or broker, he furnishes the weight or measure; (iv) provides a service which is of an unreasonably lesser quality than the service offered or represented; (v) engages in any other fraudulent business transaction which is made punishable by the laws of the State of Georgia;
(2) Violates any laws, ordinances or resolutions regulating such business;
(3) The licensee has supplied false information to the licenses and permits office or board of commissioners regardless of when the county shall have become aware of same;
(4) The licensee has failed to obtain or has suffered the expiration, suspension or revocation of any paper or document necessary to pursue its business as may be required by any office, agency, authority or department of the county, state or the United States under authority of any law, ordinance or resolution of the county, state or the United States;
(5) The licensee has failed to comply with any provisions of this article;
(6) A licensee makes any misrepresentation of fact, whether through advertisement or through any form of direct communication oral or written, which is intended to mislead the public or to mislead any party with whom the licensee deals. The term "misrepresentation of fact" as used herein shall embrace not only express misrepresentations; but, also misrepresentations arising by virtue of the licensee's conduct, including acts and omissions. By way of illustration only and without limiting the scope of this subsection, "due cause" as herein defined shall consist of any act or practice designated as unlawful in sections 3 (b)(1) through 3 (b)(11) of the Fair Business Practices Act of 1975 (OCGA 10-1-390 et seq.) or declared by the Administrator of said Act to be unlawful pursuant to regulations made under section 4 of said Act, subject to the exemptions contained in Section 6 of said Act; or
(7) Any licensee who has been charged with the offense of theft by receiving stolen property as contemplated under the provisions of OCGA section 16-8-7. It is not necessary for the licensee to be convicted under the statute.
(c) The board of commissioners may specify certain conditions of operation upon the licensee during any time of probation. Such conditions shall be on file with the licenses and permits office. No probation shall extend over a period of more than twelve (12) consecutive calendar months.
(Ord. No. 92-07, 9-1-92)

