(a) This chapter has been enacted to establish the minimum fire safety standards and requirements for the prevention of loss of life from fire, panic from fear of fire, explosions or other related hazards in all buildings, structures, and facilities. Further, this chapter provides for rules and regulations to improve public safety by promoting the control of fire hazards; regulating the use of structures; premises and open area; providing for the abatement of fire hazards; establishing the responsibilities and procedures for code enforcement; and setting forth the standards for compliance.
(b) The state minimum fire safety standards shall be enforced by the fire marshal in the fire department of the county which is hereby established and which shall be operated under the supervision of the chief of the fire department. The fire marshal shall have the duties of the chief of the bureau of fire prevention.
(c) Any authority, power or duty vested in the fire marshal by any provision of this article may be exercised, discharged or performed by a deputy, assistant or other designated individual acting in the fire marshal's name and by their delegated authority.
