(1) International Fire Code;
(2) International Building Code;
(3) National Fire Protection Association (NFPA) 101 Life Safety Code;
(4) National Fire Protection Association (NFPA) 13, 13D, 13E, and 13R Sprinkler Code;
(5) National Fire Protection Association (NFPA) 72 Alarm Code;
(6) National Fire Protection Association (NFPA) Fire Protection Handbook;
(7) National Fire Protection Association (NFPA) 111 Standard on Stored Electrical Energy Emergency and Standby Power Systems;
(8) National Fire Protection Association (NFPA) 400 Hazardous Materials Code;
(9) National Fire Protection Association (NFPA) 401 Recommended Practice for the Prevention of Fires and Uncontrolled Chemical Reactions Associated with the Handling of Hazardous Waste;
(10) National Fire Protection Association (NFPA) 484 Standard for Combustible Metals;
